{
  "id": "AJC.picrep.projective-infra",
  "status": "pending",
  "summary": "PENDING at external Picard producer gates, with the owned projective API frozen and verified. The demanded Grassmannian program is complete: Plucker immersion, projectivity/H-quasi-projectivity over Spec Z, and field-representer transport are proved and consumed by the generic D4 composition adapter. IsHQuasiProjectiveWith remains the sole carried-O(1) very-ample vocabulary. Reactivate only when D3 supplies an actual whole-fibre base locus Z and a quasi-compact immersion Z -> representingScheme, or when a represented Picard component exposes an exact relative-Proj/ample signature. Current D2 evaluation/rank/naturality and D3 locus construction are Picard-side producer work; pointedPicSharpQuasiProjectivePieces_demand still packages that missing representation and is not projective infrastructure. No duplicate Proj, ample, or very-ample declarations are authorized."
}
{
  "id": "AJC.picrep.projective-infra.ample",
  "status": "pending",
  "summary": "PENDING behind the same concrete-consumer gate. PointedPicSharpRep asks for H-quasi-projective pieces and FiniteInAffine, not an ample predicate. The live degree route has no represented component or Picard-piece line bundle yet. Activate only when such a component exposes a nonvanishing-locus or twist theorem with an exact Lean signature; do not define ample tautologically as existence of a very-ample power or duplicate IsHQuasiProjectiveWith."
}
{
  "id": "AJC.picrep.projective-infra.grassmannian",
  "status": "done",
  "summary": "DONE. The Plucker chain constructs normalized maximal-minor charts, proves overlap compatibility, glues the absolute morphism, proves local coordinate-ring surjectivity and global IsImmersion, lifts to relative projective space over Spec Z, and combines existing properness with immersion to prove Grassmannian.isProjective_toSpecZ and isHQuasiProjective_toSpecZ. Projective/Grassmannian.lean consumes the latter to prove the chosen field representer H-quasi-projective. No Fin reindex is needed because the current predicates accept any finite coordinate type. D3 still owes its actual locus/map; the generic D4 composition adapter does not claim that construction."
}
{
  "id": "AJC.picrep.projective-infra.ledger",
  "status": "done",
  "summary": "DONE as phase-0 demand accounting, now reconciled with the proved API. DemandLedger.lean retains exactly one intentional root sorry, PointedPicSharpQuasiProjectivePieces, a stronger sufficient Picard representation package rather than the minimal seam price. The closed absolute and field Grassmannian rows point directly to Grassmannian.isHQuasiProjective_toSpecZ and Scheme.Grassmannian.representingScheme_isHQuasiProjective_of_field; duplicate demand wrappers were deleted in 650b9f291c. Relative Proj and ampleness remain absent because no elaborated Picard consumer demands them."
}
{
  "id": "AJC.picrep.projective-infra.relative-proj",
  "status": "pending",
  "summary": "PENDING with no current Lean demand. Kernel probing confirms that the two former absolute section-Proj structure assemblies are elementary, but no source imports the ledger, calls Proj.fromOfGlobalSections, provides picSharpDeg, represents a component, or supplies a Picard-piece line bundle. They were removed from the seam ledger rather than counted as infrastructure progress. Activate this row only after intrinsic degree plus a real component representation exposes an exact Proj signature; do not build general sheaf-relative-Proj gluing."
}
{
  "id": "AJC.picrep.projective-infra.very-ample",
  "status": "done",
  "summary": "DONE as a vocabulary and boundary decision, not a new theorem. At Scheme.{0}, IsHQuasiProjectiveWith already records a quasi-compact projective-space immersion and identification with pulled-back O(1); it is the faithful very-ample output. The universe-polymorphic seam uses IsHQuasiProjective. No IsVeryAmple alias or duplicate transport API is permitted."
}
